course: dictionary
lesson: 10470
title: Naming things in nature
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A noun is a naming word for a person, place or thing. Tulip is a noun, and so is tulips when you mean more than one. Nouns often sit near clues that tell you more about them. «Feather grass, wild tulips and lime trees each have clever tricks to live here.» Here tulips is a plant, and the words around it show it is one of several living things.
explain: Think of a tulip as a bright spring flower shaped like a cup, growing from a bulb. When you read about it, look for the clues around the word: the season, the colour, and where it grows. «Schrenk's tulip grows wild in southern Ukraine» tells you it is not only a garden flower.
explain: Maths and science words work the same way. Counting tulips, planting bulbs and comparing colours are all tulip lessons too. Ask yourself what the sentence is about, then use the clues to find the meaning.
fact: A tulip is a noun: a naming word for a flower.
fact: Tulips grow from bulbs, which are planted in autumn and flower in spring.
fact: Tulips come in many colours, such as red, yellow, pink, white and purple.
fact: «Schrenk's tulip» grows wild in southern Ukraine and is a wild relative of garden tulips.
fact: In the 1630s, a single striped tulip bulb could cost as much as a house.
exercise: Find the plant word in «Feather grass, wild tulips and lime trees each have clever tricks to live here.» | clever | tricks | here | *tulips
exercise: Tom plants 10 tulip bulbs and 4 of them are red. How many are not red? | *6 | 10 | 4 | 14
exercise: When are tulip bulbs planted, and when do tulips flower? | Planted in spring, flower in winter | Planted in summer, flower in autumn | *Planted in autumn, flower in spring | Planted in winter, flower in summer
test: «The famous stripes on broken tulips in old Dutch paintings were caused by a virus.» What caused the stripes? | *a virus | the sun | the paint brushes | the frame around the picture
test: Which country is famous for its tulip fields? | *the Netherlands | Brazil | Scotland | Australia
exam: «Schrenk's tulip grows wild in southern Ukraine and is a wild relative of garden tulips.» Where does Schrenk's tulip grow wild? | a garden in London | Scotland | *southern Ukraine | the Netherlands
